{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@attached"},{"kind":"text","text":"(peer) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetEntry"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V","text":"UInt32"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The kind the record is tagged with, as an integer literal."}]}],"name":"kind"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach it to a static property, a global variable, a static function, a free function, or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"struct, enum, class or actor that isn’t generic, at file scope or in a type that isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generic. Anything else is a compile-time error that says why. The macro adds a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@used"},{"type":"text","text":" peer, placed with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@section"},{"type":"text","text":" in the section LinkerSets owns, whose accessor produces the variable’s value, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function itself as a value of its function type, or the type’s metatype as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Any.Type"},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSet"},{"type":"text","text":" of the same kind and value type finds it at run time:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum Routes {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x726F_7574)","    static let home = Route(path: \"\/\")","}","","let routes = LinkerSet<Route>(kind: LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)).values"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The kind is an integer literal from 1 through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt32.max"},{"type":"text","text":"; kind 0 is reserved for empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slots. A record produces its value only for a request of exactly its type: a function"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"func f(_ x: Int) -> String"},{"type":"text","text":" is found by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<(Int) -> String>"},{"type":"text","text":", and a type by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<Any.Type>"},{"type":"text","text":". A client whose types share a protocol reads them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any P.Type"},{"type":"text","text":" through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a macro of its own that requires it (LinkerSetsMacroSupport’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetMacro"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:10LinkerSets0A8SetEntry4kindys6UInt32V_tcfm","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"title":"LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","roleHeading":"Macro","remoteSource":{"fileName":"LinkerSetEntry.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/LinkerSets\/blob\/main\/Sources\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry.swift#L27"},"symbolKind":"macro","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetEntry"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UInt32","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetentry(kin